# next-sitemap writes LF regardless of platform, and these two are committed
# (see .gitignore). Without this a build on a checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# leaves them permanently "modified" in git status - identical in content, off
# by line ending - which is exactly the noise keeping them tracked is meant to
# avoid.
public/robots.txt text eol=lf
public/sitemap.xml text eol=lf
